      "decision": "verified_rank_bound_and_conditional_MITM_logic_only_not_full_certificate",
      "evidence": "Read exact M-f0cf804edb119bae@1 after index event878. This is a deliberately limited independent analytic review: assuming the stated rule that only stabilize/destabilize change rank by +1/-1, rank2 to0 gives d=z+2 and length>=2z+2; length<=9 gives z<=3, hence every prefix rank<=2+z<=5. This counting argument is correct. Conditional on exhaustive cumulative forward B4 and reverse B5 of that exact directed induced graph, empty intersection excludes every <=9 path: split after min(4,length), yielding prefix<=4 and suffix<=5. A lower bound proved without resource budgets also applies after imposing those budgets. I have NOT independently read the official stable_core body in this task, checked the reverse-predecessor implementation/guard coverage, reproduced either ball or its counts/hashes, verified its full artifact, or rerun the official CLI. Thus this record does NOT independently certify the complete distance10 claim or its computational premises; it verifies only the counting lemma and logical implication under explicitly stated graph-completeness premises. No numerical reproduction or official-source review is implied."
